00:43:23.300 --> 00:43:24.320
I know. They found it.

00:43:25.840 --> 00:43:27.560
Nick's doing a few days down there himself.

00:43:30.570 --> 00:43:31.550
What happened on the break?

00:43:31.900 --> 00:43:33.360
Ponty squealed like I said he would.

00:43:33.900 --> 00:43:35.440
Douglas and his men were waiting for him.

00:43:35.560 --> 00:43:36.120
They got him all.

00:43:37.330 --> 00:43:39.330
You weren't so bad off where you were, after all.

00:43:40.700 --> 00:43:41.520
What happened to Ponty?

00:43:41.830 --> 00:43:43.550
They got him working on the warden's office.

00:43:43.850 --> 00:43:45.730
They're trying to get him transferred to some other prison.

00:43:46.050 --> 00:43:47.310
They'll never get out alive.

00:43:48.180 --> 00:43:49.080
Mapes is dead.

00:43:49.570 --> 00:43:50.590
You should have known better.

00:43:50.710 --> 00:43:51.930
How can you know anything?

00:43:52.210 --> 00:43:53.520
Nothing makes any sense.

00:43:53.660 --> 00:43:54.480
It's always the same.

00:43:55.230 --> 00:43:57.570
The good guys get it in the neck and the rats get the gravy.

00:43:58.500 --> 00:43:59.280
Mapes is dead.

00:44:00.120 --> 00:44:02.100
Pony has a soft job in the warden's office.

00:44:02.380 --> 00:44:03.760
I don't think it'll last too long.

00:44:05.270 --> 00:44:06.870
Lupert, come on.

00:44:07.100 --> 00:44:08.120
You want it in the warden's office.

00:44:08.330 --> 00:44:09.090
What's he wanted for?

00:44:09.760 --> 00:44:10.500
Oh, didn't you know?

00:44:11.400 --> 00:44:13.240
The warden needs a fourth at bridge.

00:44:13.600 --> 00:44:15.560
Pony, he didn't check with me to see if it was okay.

00:44:15.780 --> 00:44:16.920
All right, wise guy, come on.

00:44:21.900 --> 00:44:22.620
So good, does he?

00:44:22.960 --> 00:44:24.800
He'll be all right after a couple days of food.

00:44:25.700 --> 00:44:26.860
What are we gonna do about Pony?

00:44:28.760 --> 00:44:29.980
Make his death as pain.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:35.120
this is possible but you've got to get me out of here warden i know these guys i know what

00:44:35.120 --> 00:44:40.380
they're planning right now all right ponny calm down i can't be calm how can you be calm when

00:44:40.380 --> 00:44:43.640
you're sitting right in the middle of 2500 guys and every one of them just waiting a chance to

00:44:43.640 --> 00:44:46.960
stick a shiv in your back you're not sitting in the middle of them there's eight feet of wall

00:44:46.960 --> 00:44:51.470
and a hundred guards between you but that ain't what he promised me he said i'd get out of here

00:44:51.530 --> 00:44:56.110
he promised me i'd get out you had no right to promise him anything douglas it's up to the

00:44:56.110 --> 00:44:59.980
parole board you know that deal with these things the best way you can warden yeah well i don't

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:04.760
think this is the best way i've never made deals with men like this in my life all right what happens

00:45:04.760 --> 00:45:08.820
to me now i'm gonna try and get you transferred to another prison what good will that do they'll

00:45:08.820 --> 00:45:13.500
be waiting for me there too any prison any place you've got to let me out get this through your

00:45:13.500 --> 00:45:20.340
head potty i don't know anything about the deal you and douglas made i'll do the best i can warden

00:45:20.490 --> 00:45:27.210
you don't know these men i think i do that's why i'm keeping you up here working in the office

00:45:27.210 --> 00:45:28.310
having your food sent in.

00:45:28.650 --> 00:45:29.790
I even let you sleep up here.

00:45:30.480 --> 00:45:32.620
But keep away from me, punty. I can't stand a whiner.

00:45:32.820 --> 00:45:33.280
But, Warden...

00:45:33.280 --> 00:45:33.960
That's all, Douglas.

00:45:37.920 --> 00:45:39.060
Cap, you promised me.

00:45:39.060 --> 00:45:39.320
Come on.

00:45:39.480 --> 00:45:41.020
You know you promised me.

00:45:51.010 --> 00:45:52.230
Hughford, sir. You wanted to see him.

00:45:52.580 --> 00:45:53.420
I'll see him alone.

00:45:57.980 --> 00:45:58.480
Hello, Joe.

00:46:00.090 --> 00:46:02.910
Come in, sit down.

00:46:11.420 --> 00:46:11.740
Cigarette?

00:46:13.130 --> 00:46:23.790
I have some time, Joe.

00:46:25.530 --> 00:46:26.730
Seems that way to me, too.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:31.560
I'm looking over your record. You've done pretty well here.

00:46:33.240 --> 00:46:35.320
You can call solitary doing pretty well.

00:46:36.560 --> 00:46:38.340
The guard didn't know your father had died, Joe.

00:46:40.060 --> 00:46:41.700
Would it have made any difference if he did?

00:46:43.300 --> 00:46:46.170
I think so. I don't.

00:46:49.170 --> 00:46:52.250
This is a big place. It's hard to keep track of everybody's personal problems.

00:46:52.410 --> 00:46:53.970
You managed to keep track of everything else.

00:46:54.150 --> 00:46:59.840
It was a bad break. I can be some help.

00:47:01.370 --> 00:47:03.150
I can keep it off your record when you come up for parole.

00:47:04.150 --> 00:47:05.610
It's hardly in the line of duty, is it?

00:47:07.810 --> 00:47:08.270
What do you mean?

00:47:08.890 --> 00:47:11.690
I remember you telling me a couple of times that you had a job to do.

00:47:12.820 --> 00:47:15.020
How the cards fall, that's the way you have to take them.

00:47:15.840 --> 00:47:16.380
Yeah, that's right.

00:47:17.240 --> 00:47:21.440
If I were district attorney again and your case came up, I'd prosecute you again.

00:47:21.970 --> 00:47:23.870
Then why bother to keep anything off my record?

00:47:24.640 --> 00:47:26.160
I said prosecute, not persecute.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:31.200
You'd be crazy about your father, wouldn't you?

00:47:34.180 --> 00:47:34.840
Course I was.

00:47:36.280 --> 00:47:37.800
My daughter called on him after the trial.

00:47:42.390 --> 00:47:42.910
He wrote me.

00:47:45.240 --> 00:47:48.000
Don't you think he'd want you to pull out of this, go ahead and make a life for yourself?

00:47:48.780 --> 00:47:50.100
I haven't any idea what he'd want.

00:47:50.730 --> 00:47:54.470
Joel, haven't you some kind of faith or religion?

00:47:56.130 --> 00:47:56.830
Yeah, I did have.

00:47:57.870 --> 00:47:59.390
I sprung a few leaks in this place.

00:48:00.320 --> 00:48:01.540
What are your plans when you get out of here?

00:48:03.470 --> 00:48:04.010
I haven't any.

00:48:06.170 --> 00:48:06.810
Can you drive a car?

00:48:09.060 --> 00:48:09.700
I used to.

00:48:16.500 --> 00:48:19.810
You busy? Step in here for a minute, huh?

00:48:21.780 --> 00:48:25.720
Joe, other men have had lots worse breaks than you, but they've come through them.

00:48:27.060 --> 00:48:27.720
How old are you now?

00:48:28.840 --> 00:48:29.100
29.

00:48:30.220 --> 00:48:31.580
You've got a lot behind you for 29.

00:48:31.920 --> 00:48:32.820
You've got a lot ahead of you, too.

00:48:33.930 --> 00:48:35.050
Are you going to let everything get you down?

00:48:35.730 --> 00:48:37.010
I haven't let anything happen.

00:48:37.130 --> 00:48:38.230
It's just gone ahead and done it.

00:48:44.820 --> 00:48:46.230
Hey, you remember Joe Hewford?

00:48:47.600 --> 00:48:47.920
Yes.

00:48:50.470 --> 00:48:51.210
So I'm at the trial.

00:48:52.530 --> 00:48:53.610
Joe's going to be our new chauffeur.

00:48:53.750 --> 00:48:58.250
This makes you a trustee, Joe.

00:48:58.450 --> 00:48:59.570
You'll drive me and my daughter.

00:49:00.060 --> 00:49:01.680
Do errands. It's one of the best jobs here.

00:49:03.720 --> 00:49:04.140
I know.

00:49:08.000 --> 00:49:11.670
Send in a guard. You can start tomorrow.

00:49:11.910 --> 00:49:16.680
I'll tell Captain Douglas. That's all, Joe.

00:49:34.890 --> 00:49:36.010
Doesn't seem the same, does he?

00:49:36.630 --> 00:49:37.290
No, he doesn't.

00:49:38.910 --> 00:49:40.650
He'll be coming up for parole for too long.

00:49:41.790 --> 00:49:43.330
I thought this job might be a good idea.

00:49:44.690 --> 00:49:45.730
Help him to readjust himself.

00:49:47.890 --> 00:49:48.870
You could help, too, if you would.

00:49:49.070 --> 00:49:49.290
How?

00:49:50.860 --> 00:49:52.060
Well, he's going to be driving your lap.

00:49:52.630 --> 00:49:56.160
Treat him more like someone you know rather than a convict.

00:49:57.050 --> 00:49:58.490
Draw him out. Make him talk about himself.

00:49:58.690 --> 00:49:59.030
All right.

00:50:00.440 --> 00:50:02.260
Still have him on your conscience a little bit, haven't you?

00:50:03.250 --> 00:50:04.090
No, it isn't that.

00:50:04.290 --> 00:50:07.000
It's just that he's going to be getting out of here soon,

00:50:07.020 --> 00:50:09.880
and I'd like to see that he's ready for it.

00:50:10.690 --> 00:50:12.200
Sure, Dad. I'll be glad to help.

00:50:36.200 --> 00:50:38.400
Well, I don't believe you'd be too interested in knowing her anyway.

00:50:39.460 --> 00:50:41.100
Did you think I was going to do strangling?

00:50:41.260 --> 00:50:57.590
If you're in town, you'd think they'd be used to uniforms.

00:50:58.310 --> 00:50:59.830
Not many of us have a chance to get out.

00:51:00.280 --> 00:51:05.560
prayed around did it bother you much no that's all right something to scare their children with

00:51:05.580 --> 00:51:18.190
how'd he like the car done a lot to them in three years joe you know your father was a fine man

00:51:18.190 --> 00:51:28.820
i went to see him i was a little afraid he'd resent me like that why did you go to see him

00:51:28.970 --> 00:51:29.770
oh i don't know

00:51:30.320 --> 00:51:31.880
I saw him in the courtroom during the trial.

00:51:32.670 --> 00:51:36.120
He looked so nice and so brokenhearted when you...

00:51:36.120 --> 00:51:37.660
He really appreciated your call.

00:51:38.610 --> 00:51:40.690
I've always meant to thank you for it when I got out.

00:51:41.070 --> 00:51:41.850
Now you've done it.

00:51:44.090 --> 00:51:45.670
Take the long way back if you like, Joe.

00:51:46.720 --> 00:51:47.400
Thanks, Miss Miller.

00:51:49.310 --> 00:51:50.260
No, thank you.

00:51:53.280 --> 00:51:54.980
Tell Melrose I think this pot roast is wonderful.

00:51:55.350 --> 00:51:56.950
I tasted it, sir, and I told it myself.

00:51:58.880 --> 00:51:59.960
You might tell him I enjoyed it.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:11.780
Enjoyed it too? Yes sir. How did it go today? Not so good. You've got to get Joe out of that prison

00:52:11.780 --> 00:52:16.740
uniform the next time we go into town. What happened? That didn't make him feel too welcome.

00:52:19.100 --> 00:52:22.520
I should have thought of that myself. We'll have to get him some kind of regular suit.

00:52:30.090 --> 00:52:31.250
What's the matter, Martha? You're not eating much.

00:52:31.660 --> 00:52:34.660
I fixed myself a little snack about an hour ago.

00:52:35.920 --> 00:52:36.300
Why?

00:52:37.500 --> 00:52:40.690
Well, you can trust that cook if you want to.

00:52:40.990 --> 00:52:43.760
But when I think of his poor dead wife,

00:52:44.620 --> 00:52:46.700
poison gasping for breaths.

00:52:49.710 --> 00:52:51.270
Well, there's another good meal shot.

00:53:19.200 --> 00:53:21.240
Well, Joe, how are things in the great outside world?

00:53:22.000 --> 00:53:25.300
People are still living, eating, dying, having babies.

00:53:26.130 --> 00:53:27.250
They're just one up on us.

00:53:27.620 --> 00:53:28.240
Nice job.

00:53:29.590 --> 00:53:29.970
Driving a...

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:32.380
A pretty girl around all day in her old man's car.

00:53:32.830 --> 00:53:34.850
I don't know guys that'll break in here for a job like that.

00:53:35.120 --> 00:53:36.020
How do you get along with her?

00:53:38.850 --> 00:53:40.150
Better than just all right.

00:53:42.200 --> 00:53:42.900
What do you expect?

00:53:43.570 --> 00:53:44.690
I'm not even hired help.

00:53:45.690 --> 00:53:47.530
You're not so bad looking, Joe.

00:53:48.880 --> 00:53:52.160
Nothing to what I was when I was your age, but still not too bad.

00:53:53.010 --> 00:53:54.030
You should have seen me.

00:53:54.750 --> 00:53:56.070
We're back in 1910.

00:53:56.070 --> 00:53:57.370
Tell us about it some night, Curly.

00:54:08.250 --> 00:54:09.230
How about find some guards?

00:54:10.090 --> 00:54:15.440
Tell me, Joe, you're running a potty lately.

00:54:16.040 --> 00:54:16.680
Just once.

00:54:17.090 --> 00:54:18.110
He's scared stiff.

00:54:18.350 --> 00:54:19.310
He's got reason to be.

00:54:19.450 --> 00:54:19.570
Shh.

00:54:33.150 --> 00:54:35.210
You're going to have a hard time getting to Ponty.

00:54:35.370 --> 00:54:39.050
I think it can be handled when the time comes.

00:54:41.030 --> 00:54:41.790
When's the time?

00:54:42.400 --> 00:54:43.900
Right soon. We'll let you know.

00:54:44.040 --> 00:54:44.540
No, we won't.

00:54:45.960 --> 00:54:46.840
We're keeping him out of it.

00:55:01.150 --> 00:55:02.230
Just put them on the sink, Joe.

00:55:07.630 --> 00:55:08.270
Where is everybody?

00:55:08.800 --> 00:55:10.080
They're probably at the ball game.

00:55:10.560 --> 00:55:10.760
Where?

00:55:11.200 --> 00:55:13.340
Two of our teams are playing in the yard today.

00:55:13.560 --> 00:55:14.780
Everybody gets out to see them.

00:55:15.150 --> 00:55:16.190
Oh, I'm sorry, Joe.

00:55:16.350 --> 00:55:18.190
If I had known, I could have driven myself today.

00:55:18.860 --> 00:55:20.640
I've seen plenty of baseball games.

00:55:23.000 --> 00:55:24.720
Rose, I should start getting things ready for dinner.

00:55:24.900 --> 00:55:25.780
That's a good idea.

00:55:26.000 --> 00:55:29.250
If you like, I'll do the potatoes.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:31.040
The loss of how many fingers?

00:55:31.180 --> 00:55:31.780
What do you mean?

00:55:32.350 --> 00:55:34.470
You're talking to a man who worked his way through college.

00:55:36.560 --> 00:55:39.350
Joe, did you know that Dad's working on your parole?

00:55:41.660 --> 00:55:42.280
Yeah, he told me.

00:55:42.980 --> 00:55:44.880
He thinks the board should act on it in a couple of weeks.

00:55:45.120 --> 00:55:51.930
He seemed very excited about it.

00:55:53.110 --> 00:55:53.670
That isn't that.

00:55:53.910 --> 00:55:55.140
What's the matter?

00:55:55.300 --> 00:55:58.540
What am I going to do when I get out of here?

00:55:59.640 --> 00:55:59.960
I'm going to take it.

00:56:00.030 --> 00:56:04.450
a chance with me. Can't you go back to the firm you were working for? I don't think they're too

00:56:04.450 --> 00:56:09.370
interested in hex cons and a brokerage house. Well, why should it make any difference to them?

00:56:09.760 --> 00:56:16.000
It's all over and done with. You've already paid whatever debt you owed. Would you feel that way

00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:21.790
about it? Of course I would. Joe, there are people who've done much worse than you did walking the

00:56:21.790 --> 00:56:29.970
streets right now. Without a record, all the guys I've talked to tell me it's no cinch. That's why a lot of

00:56:30.600 --> 00:56:36.280
I don't think so.

00:56:37.120 --> 00:56:38.860
The question is, what am I going to do?

00:56:40.340 --> 00:56:42.440
I'm not even a citizen anymore.

00:56:47.990 --> 00:56:49.270
What were you studying before the war?

00:56:51.140 --> 00:56:52.160
Business administration.

00:56:53.990 --> 00:56:54.910
I'll talk to Dad about it.

00:56:55.620 --> 00:56:56.260
Not his problem.

00:56:58.300 --> 00:56:58.960
Maybe it is.

00:57:05.820 --> 00:57:07.700
It really wouldn't make any difference to you.

00:57:10.480 --> 00:57:11.080
Not a bit.

00:57:14.330 --> 00:57:15.510
Very important to me someday.

00:57:16.590 --> 00:57:19.090
If it is, then you can count on it.

00:57:31.240 --> 00:57:33.360
I don't like it, Warden. The whole prison's too quiet.

00:57:34.120 --> 00:57:35.500
Believe me, they're up to something.

00:57:36.190 --> 00:57:36.470
Potty?

00:57:36.900 --> 00:57:37.220
Sure.

00:57:38.430 --> 00:57:40.330
I know he's up here. They wouldn't try to get through to him, would they?

00:57:40.550 --> 00:57:41.690
You never know what they're planning.

00:57:42.000 --> 00:57:43.760
When they're too quiet, you can be sure it's something.

00:57:46.490 --> 00:57:46.790
Come in.

00:57:49.340 --> 00:57:51.520
Sorry to break in, Dad, but I've got to catch the train.

00:57:52.180 --> 00:57:53.420
Joe's going to drive me to the station.

00:57:54.250 --> 00:57:55.910
I don't believe your aunt. Elena's really sick.

00:57:56.010 --> 00:57:57.190
I think she just wants to see you.

00:57:58.200 --> 00:57:59.180
Can I get you anything in the city?

00:58:00.160 --> 00:58:01.740
No, just say hello to your aunt for me, huh?

00:58:02.550 --> 00:58:03.810
Sure, Dad. Bye.

00:58:04.940 --> 00:58:08.740
Kay, how long are you going to be gone?

00:58:09.000 --> 00:58:09.620
About a week.

00:58:09.840 --> 00:58:10.420
I'm going to miss you.

00:58:10.620 --> 00:58:10.940
Me too.

00:58:12.420 --> 00:58:14.460
Tell Huford I want to see him just as soon as he gets back, will you?

00:58:15.350 --> 00:58:15.710
All right.

00:58:22.610 --> 00:58:23.890
I'm just as glad she's getting away.

00:58:24.400 --> 00:58:25.180
Take a look, Warden.

00:58:32.270 --> 00:58:33.810
I've got the guards trying to keep them moving.

00:58:34.700 --> 00:58:37.660
But you bust up one bunch, you get another one behind your back right away.

00:58:57.230 --> 00:58:58.600
Come on, keep moving.

00:59:04.250 --> 00:59:05.410
Come on, break it up.

00:59:14.320 --> 00:59:14.820
1.30.

00:59:19.710 --> 00:59:20.600
1.30.

00:59:20.800 --> 00:59:22.500
All right, break it up, break it up.

00:59:32.200 --> 00:59:34.480
Cut the conversation. Keep working.

00:59:54.970 --> 00:59:56.150
We've got a few minutes yet.

00:59:56.530 --> 00:59:57.150
Good for us.

01:00:02.240 --> 01:00:11.310
Come on, Joe. Here's a bench. Sit down.

01:00:13.220 --> 01:00:15.570
Not yet. Maybe in a few weeks.

01:00:16.420 --> 01:00:17.020
That's simply.

01:00:17.760 --> 01:00:20.810
Not to me. How long are you going to be gone?

01:00:21.520 --> 01:00:24.130
Oh, about a week. Is there anything I can do for you?

01:00:25.260 --> 01:00:29.620
Yeah, I might... I'll tell you what, you might put an ad in the newspaper for me.

01:00:30.510 --> 01:00:36.650
One ex-convict with plans for the future needs a good job to carry out those plans.

01:00:38.360 --> 01:00:39.060
What plans, Joe?

01:00:43.170 --> 01:00:47.590
Sitting by your first name sometimes.

01:00:49.020 --> 01:00:50.360
Nobody's ever stopped you from doing that.

01:01:18.360 --> 01:01:18.860
Have a good time.

01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:20.150
Carry home.

01:01:20.270 --> 01:01:21.130
Thanks again, I will.

01:01:24.800 --> 01:01:27.230
No, people aren't all alike.

01:01:28.090 --> 01:01:29.960
What I mean is, the woman who walked around...

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:44.680
you that day downtown. Everybody doesn't feel that way. Understand what I mean? Yeah, I hope I do.

01:02:23.800 --> 01:02:25.170
Oh, coffee.

01:02:26.300 --> 01:02:29.720
Well, now that it's here...

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:41.800
right i wish you wouldn't walk so quietly i never hear you coming and i never hear you going

01:02:41.800 --> 01:02:46.460
yes anything else madam no

01:03:04.830 --> 01:03:12.480
Potty, put those away.

01:03:13.630 --> 01:03:17.560
What are you so nervous about?

01:03:18.830 --> 01:03:19.250
I don't know.

01:03:20.320 --> 01:03:22.440
That room you sleep in has no exit except through this office.

01:03:22.600 --> 01:03:24.020
There's no one around except my servants.

01:03:24.640 --> 01:03:27.300
Do you think they're going to risk the easy jobs they've got to say nothing of their necks?

01:03:28.000 --> 01:03:29.060
They're going to get me, Warden.

01:03:30.030 --> 01:03:38.920
